# Windows 11 Pro product keys, one per VM.
#
#   cp keys/product-keys.env.example keys/product-keys.env    (git-ignored)
#
# Format: <vm-name>=XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX
# DEFAULT is used for any VM without its own line. Leave a value empty to run
# that VM unactivated (fine for testing). One retail key activates one machine,
# so give each VM its own key unless you have volume/MAK licensing.
#
# setup.sh / make-oem.sh copy the key into that VM's OEM folder only. The VM
# installs it on first boot, activates through the egress proxy, then deletes
# the copy from C:\OEM.

DEFAULT=
app-a=
app-b=
